<%= render "shared/page_header",
      title: "Elephants in Pop Culture",
      intro: "Elephants are stars! You can find them in books, cartoons and movies. Meet some famous elephants, " \
             "then find out what real elephants can do." %>

<div class="section kids" data-controller="load-more" data-load-more-per-page-value="3">
  <span class="section-label">Famous elephants</span>
  <div class="kid-grid">
    <% [
      ["Dumbo", "🐘🪶", "kid-card--sky", "A Disney movie",
       "Dumbo is a baby elephant with very big ears. Everyone laughs at his ears, until he uses them to fly!",
       "Real elephants can't fly. But they flap their big ears to cool down on hot days.",
       "Learn about elephant ears", anatomy_path],
      ["Babar", "👑🐘", "kid-card--sun", "A picture book",
       "Babar is a little elephant who grows up to be king. He wears a smart green suit and a crown.",
       "Real elephant families are led by a grandma elephant called the matriarch.",
       "Learn about elephant families", behavior_path],
      ["Horton", "🐘🌸", "kid-card--pink", "A Dr. Seuss book",
       "Horton hears tiny people living on a speck of dust. He says: \"A person's a person, no matter how small.\"",
       "Real elephants have amazing hearing. They can even feel sounds through their feet!",
       "Learn how elephants talk", behavior_path],
      ["Elmer", "🐘🌈", "kid-card--rainbow", "A picture book",
       "Elmer is a patchwork elephant covered in bright colours. He is funny and loves to make his friends laugh.",
       "Real elephants are grey. They roll in mud and dust to protect their skin from the sun.",
       "Learn about elephant skin", anatomy_path],
      ["Gerald", "🐘🐷", "kid-card--leaf", "Elephant & Piggie books",
       "Gerald is an elephant who worries a lot. His best friend is Piggie, and they always help each other.",
       "Real elephants have best friends too. They say hello by wrapping their trunks together.",
       "Learn about elephant friends", behavior_path],
      ["Colonel Hathi", "🐘🥁", "kid-card--sand", "The Jungle Book",
       "Colonel Hathi leads his elephant troop on a marching parade through the jungle. Hup, two, three, four!",
       "\"Hathi\" means \"elephant\" in Hindi. Real Asian elephants live in the forests of India.",
       "Learn where elephants live", habitat_path],
      ["Manny", "🦣❄️", "kid-card--ice", "The Ice Age movies",
       "Manny is a woolly mammoth. He is big, grumpy on the outside and kind on the inside.",
       "Mammoths are elephant cousins that lived long ago. They had thick hairy coats to stay warm.",
       "Learn about elephant cousins", classification_path]
    ].each_with_index do |(name, picture, colour, from, story, real_fact, link_label, path), index| %>
      <div class="kid-card <%= colour %>" data-load-more-target="item" <%= "hidden" if index >= 3 %>
           data-mascot-label="Real elephant fact" data-mascot-fact="<%= real_fact %>">
        <div class="kid-picture" role="img" aria-label="Picture of <%= name %>"><%= picture %></div>
        <h3><%= name %></h3>
        <span class="kid-from"><%= from %></span>
        <p><%= story %></p>
        <%# Ellie pops this fact up on hover; the printed copy is only shown where she can't (touch devices) %>
        <p class="kid-real"><strong>Real elephant fact:</strong> <%= real_fact %></p>
        <%= link_to "#{link_label} →", path, class: "kid-link" %>
      </div>
    <% end %>
  </div>
  <div class="load-more">
    <button type="button" class="kid-link" data-load-more-target="button" data-action="load-more#more">
      Show more elephants 🐘
    </button>
  </div>
</div>

<div class="section kids">
  <span class="section-label">Did you know?</span>
  <div class="highlight-box">
    <p>
      <strong>Jumbo size!</strong> Long ago, there was a real elephant named Jumbo. He was so big and so famous
      that people started saying "jumbo" to mean "really big". So a jumbo jet is named after an elephant!
    </p>
  </div>
</div>

<div class="section kids">
  <span class="section-label">Your turn</span>
  <div class="kid-card kid-card--sun kid-card--wide">
    <div class="kid-picture" role="img" aria-label="Crayons and paper">🖍️📄</div>
    <h3>Make your own elephant!</h3>
    <p>
      Grab some paper and crayons. Draw your very own elephant character. What is its name? What colour is it?
      Does it have a special power, like flying or super hearing?
    </p>
    <%= link_to "See real elephant photos for ideas →", gallery_index_path, class: "kid-link" %>
  </div>
</div>
